[
    {
        "content": "<p>I noticed that some of the lemmas are called Int.divisorsAntidiagonal and others are Int.divisorsAntidiag :(</p>",
        "id": 588744768,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ang",
        "timestamp": 1776816335
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We should unify the names of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.divisorsAntidiagonal#doc\">docs#Nat.divisorsAntidiagonal</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Int.divisorsAntidiag#doc\">docs#Int.divisorsAntidiag</a></p>",
        "id": 588745562,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776816491
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Probably there's a poll somewhere</p>",
        "id": 588745589,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776816495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/21912\">#21912</a> introduced the short <code>Int</code> version, the long <code>Nat</code> version is from mathlib3 (<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib/pull/4310\">!3#4310</a>)</p>",
        "id": 588752304,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776818265
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.divisorsAntidiagonalList#doc\">docs#Nat.divisorsAntidiagonalList</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.Nat.antidiagonal#doc\">docs#List.Nat.antidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Multiset.Nat.antidiagonal#doc\">docs#Multiset.Nat.antidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Multiset.antidiagonal#doc\">docs#Multiset.antidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.antidiagonal#doc\">docs#Finset.antidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.antidiagonal#doc\">docs#Set.antidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.HasAntidiagonal#doc\">docs#Finset.HasAntidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.HasMulAntidiagonal#doc\">docs#Finset.HasMulAntidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.Nat.antidiagonalTuple#doc\">docs#List.Nat.antidiagonalTuple</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Multiset.Nat.antidiagonalTuple#doc\">docs#Multiset.Nat.antidiagonalTuple</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.Nat.antidiagonalTuple#doc\">docs#Finset.Nat.antidiagonalTuple</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.finAntidiagonal#doc\">docs#Finset.finAntidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.mulAntidiagonal#doc\">docs#Finset.mulAntidiagonal</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.piAntidiag#doc\">docs#Finset.piAntidiag</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.finsuppAntidiag#doc\">docs#Finset.finsuppAntidiag</a></p>\n<p>Well we're definitely not consistent, but it looks like the long version is winning so far (12 vs 3)<br>\n(the two <code>Finset</code> short versions were added in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/13683\">#13683</a>)</p>",
        "id": 588753028,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776818760
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span> any opinions on this?</p>",
        "id": 590160250,
        "sender_full_name": "David Ang",
        "timestamp": 1776851635
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>6 messages were moved here from <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Computable.20.60Fintype.20.7Ba.20.3A.20.E2.84.95.20.2F.2F.20a.20.E2.88.A3.20n.7D.60.20for.20.60fin_cases.60\">#Is there code for X? &gt; Computable &#96;Fintype {a : ℕ // a ∣ n}&#96; for &#96;fin_cases&#96;</a> by <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span>.</p>",
        "id": 590234618,
        "sender_full_name": "Notification Bot",
        "timestamp": 1776869985
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"387244\">Yaël Dillies</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Integer.20Divisors.3F/near/532545587\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The plan here is to rename <code>divisorsAntidiagonal</code> to <code>divisorsAntidiag</code>. I was waiting on <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/21915\">#21915</a> to be done before doing so, but I think it's not going to be ready anytime soon, so feel free to rename <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.divisorsAntidiagonal#doc\">docs#Nat.divisorsAntidiagonal</a> now!</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 590234841,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776870030
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>btw, what about <code>diag</code> vs <code>diagonal</code>? <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.diagonal#doc\">docs#Set.diagonal</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.offDiag#doc\">docs#Set.offDiag</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.offDiag#doc\">docs#List.offDiag</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Finset.offDiag#doc\">docs#Finset.offDiag</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Sym2.diagSet#doc\">docs#Sym2.diagSet</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.diag#doc\">docs#Matrix.diag</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.diagonal#doc\">docs#Matrix.diagonal</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38380\">#38380</a></p>",
        "id": 590312504,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776895993
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm strongly in favor of the long version, which is easier to discover and to read.</p>",
        "id": 592692217,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1777887908
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Strangely I prefer <code>antidiagonal</code> to <code>antidiag</code>, but <code>diag</code> to <code>diagonal</code> (at least sometimes).<br>\nSpecifically I think <code>Matrix.diag</code> is nice. We like <code>rfl</code>/<code>refl</code>/<code>symm</code>/<code>trans</code>/<code>mono</code>/<code>comp</code>/<code>re</code>/<code>im</code>/<code>hom</code>/<code>iso</code>/<code>equiv</code>/<code>congr</code>/<code>coe</code>/<code>eq</code>/<code>ne</code>/<code>le</code>/<code>prod</code>/<code>mul</code>/<code>pow</code>, so why not <code>diag</code>.</p>",
        "id": 592702575,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777891334
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>OTOH I think <code>Matrix.toLin</code> should be <code>Matrix.toLinearMap</code> (<span aria-label=\"hot pepper\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f336\" role=\"img\" title=\"hot pepper\">:hot_pepper:</span>)</p>",
        "id": 592702631,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777891351
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that we have both <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.diag#doc\">docs#Matrix.diag</a> and also <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.diagonal#doc\">docs#Matrix.diagonal</a>, which compose to the identity</p>",
        "id": 592704832,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1777892022
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think that the first should be <code>Matrix.diagonal</code> and the second, <code>Matrix.ofDiagonal</code>.</p>",
        "id": 592705580,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1777892254
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A more cursed option would be to copy numpy and have a single name for both functions, via a type class to do the dispatch</p>",
        "id": 593579084,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1778173612
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479359\">Michael Stoll</span> <a href=\"#narrow/stream/287929-mathlib4/topic/antidiagonal.20vs.20antidiag/near/592705580\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think that the first should be <code>Matrix.diagonal</code> and the second, <code>Matrix.ofDiagonal</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This has the downside of giving the far more useful operation the longer name</p>",
        "id": 593579342,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1778173685
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed, that would be very cursed.</p>",
        "id": 593584615,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1778175137
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that long names strike back when you need something like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ContinuousMultilinearMap.compContinuousLinearMapL#doc\">docs#ContinuousMultilinearMap.compContinuousLinearMapL</a> where the trailing <code>L</code> should probably be replaced by something like <code>AsContinuousLinearMap</code>, if we go for long names.</p>",
        "id": 593588585,
        "sender_full_name": "Yury G. Kudryashov",
        "timestamp": 1778176240
    }
]